  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far (config_037: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, 0.706 acc) establishes that learned RNA encoders (scvi_n200 > pca_n2000) and a strong image encoder (ViT-L > ResNet50) both contribute meaningfully. However, we have not yet tested scgpt in any multimodal setting, leaving uncertainty about whether the RNA encoder dimension is saturated among learned encoders or whether scgpt's different pretraining objective could yield further gains. Question: Does scgpt, in the otherwise-best multimodal configuration (imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted), match or exceed scvi_n200's performance? Why this is the best next experiment: It directly probes the most impactful remaining design axis (RNA encoder quality) in the strongest known context, so the result will either confirm scvi_n200 as the optimal encoder (focusing future effort on other dimensions) or reveal a new promising direction. This is more informative than re-testing aggregation (avgpool already dominates transformer by ~7 pts in RNA-only) or profile setting (multiprofile clearly superior), both of which have strong existing evidence."
}

